course: dictionary
lesson: 10846
title: Vertical
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Vertical means going straight up and down, at a right angle to the flat ground. Think of a wall, a flagpole or a tall tree trunk. «The Alpine ibex climb the almost vertical stone walls of dams» means the walls are so steep they almost go straight up.
explain: A vertical line is a straight up-and-down line. The opposite of vertical is horizontal, which means flat and lying side to side, like the ground or the top of a table.
explain: You will meet vertical in maths, science and PE. In maths, the vertical axis of a graph is the y-axis. In PE, a vertical jump is a jump straight up into the air.
fact: Vertical means going straight up and down.
fact: Vertical is the opposite of horizontal.
fact: The vertical axis on a graph is the y-axis.
fact: «Foxes have vertical slit pupils like cats, which close tight in sun and open wide in the dark.» A slit pupil is a thin line standing straight up and down.
fact: «Baby ibex can climb within days of being born.» Ibex have hooves with hard edges and soft pads that grip the rock.
exercise: «The Alpine ibex climb the almost vertical stone walls of dams.» What does vertical mean here? | Round and smooth | Flat along the ground | *Straight up and down | Sloping gently
exercise: What is the opposite of vertical? | Diagonal | Upside down | Round | *Horizontal
exercise: In a maths graph, which axis is the vertical axis? | *The y-axis | The top edge of the page | The line that goes across the middle | The x-axis
test: «Foxes have vertical slit pupils, like cats.» What shape are the vertical pupils? | Square like a box | *Thin and tall, standing straight up and down | Round like a ball | Wavy like a snake
test: In PE, a vertical jump means jumping... | Sideways along the line | Backwards over a bench | Forward across the mat | *Straight up into the air
exam: Which of these things is vertical? | A road on a flat map | *A flagpole standing upright | A puddle on the floor | A table top lying flat
